TinyUSB vendored sources — DO NOT EDIT except sam3x/ port + tusb_option.h/tusb_mcu.h SAM3X entries.

Config layout (Arduino-local, not upstream):
- src/tusb_config_arduinotinyusb.h is the ONLY config the stack reads
  (src/tusb_config.h includes it; src/tusb_option.h includes that). It is a
  one-line include of config/tusb_config_union.h.
- src/config/tusb_config_union.h — full union preset (device+host, all classes),
  the shipped default and the restore point.
- src/config/tusb_config_common.h — board/MCU/OS/queues/buffers/audio/debug,
  shared by the union preset and every per-example template.
- examples/<Name>/tusb_config_arduinotinyusb.h — INERT single-role template per
  example. Not read where it sits; copy over src/tusb_config_arduinotinyusb.h to
  activate. Restore with config/tusb_config_union.h.
- -DARDUINO_TINYUSB_CONFIG_FILE="<abs path>" (src/tusb_option.h) still selects a
  config directly, and is what the CI matrix uses to compile-check templates.
